        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is KOS protein powder healthy and clean?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "By ingredient standards, it is cleaner than most: USDA Organic, Non-GMO Project Verified per KOS, no dairy, soy, gluten, sucralose or erythritol, and only 2 g of added sugar. The trade-offs are 330 mg of sodium and 4 g of saturated fat per serving, and only 20 g of protein. Healthy depends on how it fits your overall diet."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does KOS protein powder contain lead?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It can contain trace amounts, as most plant proteins do. KOS says plants absorb lead and other metals from soil, that it tests for lead, arsenic, cadmium and mercury, and that some of its products carry a California Prop 65 warning where required. Use the KOS COA lookup with your lot number to see your batch's results."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is KOS protein powder vegan, and what sweeteners does it use?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "KOS describes the protein as vegan and plant-based, made without dairy, and its protein comes from pea, flax, quinoa, pumpkin seed and chia. It is not certified vegan by an outside body that we found. The flavored versions use organic coconut sugar, stevia and monk fruit; the unflavored tub has no sweeteners."
          }
