        <div id="reviews" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            8. What Do KOS Protein Powder Reviews Say About Taste and Mixing?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Buyer reviews of KOS are mostly positive, with vanilla rated more consistently than chocolate. On KOS.com, the 28-serving vanilla tub had 1,114 reviews when we checked, 83% of them five stars and about 5% one or two stars. The chocolate tub had 834 reviews, 71% five stars and about 12% one or two stars. Those are the brand's own review widgets, so treat them as a guide to the pattern rather than an independent score.
          </p>

          <p>
            The praise repeats a few themes. Buyers report that vanilla is mild and not overly sweet, that both core flavors blend into coffee, oats and smoothies, and that KOS tastes better than many plant proteins they have tried. Several reviewers mention buying it because they are allergic to dairy or breastfeeding a baby with a milk allergy, and others like that it keeps them full between meals.
          </p>

          <p>
            The complaints are just as consistent. The most common is texture: buyers describe the chocolate as thick, gritty or sandy, say it cakes on the sides of a shaker, or say it does not dissolve well in cold water. Some report a diet-style aftertaste that they attribute to the stevia and monk fruit. A smaller group says the taste varied from one tub to the next, and a few say the powder tasted different from what they bought in earlier years. Price comes up often, with one-word reviews such as too expensive.
          </p>

          <p>
            The practical fixes buyers suggest are worth passing on. Blend rather than shake, use a non-dairy milk instead of water, and add frozen banana or a spoon of nut butter to cover the earthy edge. If you want to sample before committing, the 10-serving tubs or single-serve packets are the low-risk route. We have not tasted KOS ourselves; everything in this section is what buyers report.
          </p>
