        <div id="who-should-buy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            10. Who Should Buy KOS Protein Powder, and Who Should Skip It?
          </h2>

          <p>
            KOS is a good fit for people who want an organic, dairy-free protein for smoothies, oats and baking, and who care more about the ingredient list than the price. It suits buyers avoiding dairy, soy, gluten, sucralose and erythritol, and anyone who likes being able to look up a batch COA. It is also a reasonable choice for people who want a small vitamin and mineral boost from their shake, since one serving supplies a meaningful share of iron, B12, selenium and zinc.
          </p>

          <p>
            It is a weaker choice for lifters chasing protein per dollar. Twenty grams per serving is on the low side for a post-workout shake, and most research on muscle protein synthesis points to 20 to 40 g per meal depending on body size and age. Older adults in particular tend to need the higher end. If you want to work out your own target, use our <a href="/how-much-protein-do-i-need/">how much protein do I need</a> guide; you may find you need a bigger scoop, which raises the cost further.
          </p>

          <p>
            Skip KOS if you are a drug-tested athlete, because it carries no NSF Certified for Sport or Informed Sport certification. Skip it, or at least talk to a doctor first, if you are on a sodium-restricted diet or have kidney disease, given the 330 mg of sodium per serving. Anyone with a coconut allergy should note the coconut milk powder, and KOS products are made in facilities that also handle common allergens, per a retailer listing, so people with severe allergies should check with the brand.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you want KOS's sweetener profile without the price, the unflavored tub plus your own fruit is the cheapest route within the line. If organic is the only must-have, Orgain is cheaper. And if you want a broader list of organic options, our <a href="/best-organic-protein-powder/">best organic protein powder</a> guide ranks them by cost per 25 g and testing status.
          </p>
        </div>

